# VM Deployment Guide (`e2-micro`) — {{project_name}}

Target host profile: **GCP `e2-micro`** (~1 GB total RAM, ~378 MB safe steady-state application budget after kernel, `systemd`, `journald`, `sshd`, and monitoring overhead).

## 1. Memory Budget Checklist

| Component | Target Budget | Controls |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Linux kernel + OS services (`systemd`, `journald`, `sshd`) | ~500–600 MB | Cap `SystemMaxUse=100M` in `/etc/systemd/journald.conf` |
| `{{project_name}}.service` steady-state RSS | <= 220 MB | `MALLOC_ARENA_MAX=2`, `MemoryHigh=220M`, `MemoryMax=300M` |
| Swap / OOM safety margin | 1–2 GB swapfile | `OOMScoreAdjust=-100` protects critical service over transient helpers |

## 2. Install & Enable `systemd` Unit

```bash
sudo useradd --system --no-create-home --shell /usr/sbin/nologin {{project_name}} || true
sudo mkdir -p /opt/{{project_name}}/bin /var/lib/{{project_name}} /etc/{{project_name}}
sudo chown -R {{project_name}}:{{project_name}} /var/lib/{{project_name}}
sudo cp deploy/{{project_name}}.service /etc/systemd/system/{{project_name}}.service
sudo systemctl daemon-reload
sudo systemctl enable --now {{project_name}}.service
```

## 3. Logs & Live Resource Inspection

```bash
sudo systemctl status {{project_name}}.service
sudo journalctl -u {{project_name}}.service -n 100 --no-pager
sudo journalctl -u {{project_name}}.service -f
systemctl show {{project_name}}.service -p MemoryCurrent -p NRestarts
```

## 4. Soak Test Checklist (Before Production Cutover)

1. Verify `MemoryCurrent` stabilizes well below `220M` after 24 hours of representative load.
2. Confirm `NRestarts` remains `0` and `journalctl -k` shows zero OOM-killer events.
3. Run `sudo BACKUP_DIR=/var/backups/{{project_name}} bash deploy/backup.sh` and verify archive readability.

## 5. Rollback Procedure

```bash
sudo systemctl stop {{project_name}}.service
# Restore previous binary into /opt/{{project_name}}/bin/{{project_name}}
# Restore SQLite/data snapshot from /var/backups/{{project_name}}/ if schema changed
sudo systemctl start {{project_name}}.service
sudo journalctl -u {{project_name}}.service -n 50 --no-pager
```
